.TH ag-agent-reap 1  "reap 0.2.0-rc.3" 
.SH NAME
ag\-agent\-reap \- Abandon runs with no recent heartbeat and release their leases
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag agent reap\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Abandon runs with no recent heartbeat and release their leases
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR
Heartbeat timeout (default 10m here; with `\-\-remote`, the server\*(Aqs `agents.run_stale_after_secs`)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Say what would be abandoned without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR [\fI<NAME>\fR]
Reap the runs of a server instead of this repository (needs `agent.operate` there; without a NAME: origin). The server also revokes the credentials bound to the reaped runs
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0\-rc.3
